IDEA PIN — ordered store index: `std/indexes:ordered(<store>, <col>)` (spelling PROVISIONAL) declares an index whose distinct keys are sorted, so range guards (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`) on the indexed column route instead of sweeping, and a routed walk visits in ascending key order (join order within a bucket). `==` routes through the same directory — one index slot, the ordered declaration is the stronger structure; `std/indexes:store` stays the equality-only spelling.

Implementation shape (2026-10-26 discussion, unimplemented): the seam already exists — `guardKey`/`guardRoute` in store.index.kz is the single route-vs-scan decision and `__index_<col>` is private to the index part, so an ordered variant is a widening, not a parallel mechanism. At store scale the honest directory is a sorted key array + binary search over per-key member lists (better cache shape than any tree); a B-tree earns the slot only if the distinct-key domain outgrows a flat directory. `std/indexes:ordered` must emit both the directory AND the member buckets so the `==` consumers (`! first`, `! query`, keyed addressing if honored) share one maintenance path.

Maintenance contract pinned by input.k: `stored` writes to the ordered column move membership eagerly; `take` inside a routed range walk leaves dead members readers skip; the non-indexed-column floor still sweeps in dense order. The one semantic CHANGE this pin carries, deliberately: `! first` under a routed range answers the first member of the index's visit order (lowest matching key), not the lowest dense match — the same "first = first of the walk" contract the equality route already runs.

Creditor: none live — today's `>=` guards sweep correctly in dense order, so nothing is broken. The pin exists so the first range-predicate workload (spatial windows, time-ordered scans, render/priority order) meets a contract instead of an unexamined sweep. Bbtree (XiangpengHao/bbtree, 2026-10-23) was the prompt for this pin; its actual contributions — inline keys, optimistic latch coupling, mmap layout — answer questions this seam does not ask at koru scale.
